dsbouma@cs.vu.nl (Bouman DS) writes:

>xterm would display the 128-159 range of characters, but it won't. Does
>anyone know why, by any chance ?

Argh.  I used to have this problem and then I fixed it.  I can't
remember what I did.  I think something is stripping the high bit.
If you have IBMgraphics set (see below) it is not nethack.


The following applied only if you are using tty graphics.

If you have ASCIIGRAPH (a compile option) defined, then when nethack
updates the map, it will put the terminal into graphics mode, strip
the high bit, and print the character.  The exception to this is
if the option IBMgraphics is set.  Then it just prints out a raw
8 bit character.  If you do not have ASCIIGRAPH compiled in, the
characters are printed out the character unchecked and unmodified.



